#%PAM-1.0

# Opt-in only: `yubikey-auth setup --with-hyprlock` deploys this, and plain
# `setup` deliberately does not. With a touch-only credential this weakens the
# lock screen rather than strengthening it, because anyone standing at the
# machine can unlock it with a tap while the key is plugged in. It is worth
# deploying when the credential requires the key's own fingerprint or PIN.
#
# Submit an empty prompt to use the key, or type the account password to go
# through the unchanged login stack.
auth       sufficient                  pam_u2f.so          authfile=/etc/u2f_mappings cue origin=pam://Kelper appid=pam://Kelper userpresence=1 pinverification=0 userverification=0
auth       include                     login
